## Preamble

HashDrop is a browser-native, decentralized publishing, verification, proof, and cryptographic-content system built on Solana. It includes, among other things, the HashDrop V3 protocol with PUBLIC, PROOF, and PRIVATE publication modes, on-chain publication through Solana transactions and SPL Memo instructions, SHA-256 content hashing and verification, cryptographic commitments, client-side cryptographic operations (including AES-256-GCM, ML-KEM-768, and HKDF-SHA-256), wallet-signed transactions, and encrypted private artifacts.

This License makes the HashDrop source code available so that individuals and organizations may inspect it, learn from it, use it for non-commercial purposes, study and audit its security, and modify it for permitted purposes, while requiring that distributed derivatives of the Covered Software remain available under reciprocal terms and reserving all commercial exploitation for separate written authorization from the Licensor.

Nothing in this License grants any rights in any third-party technology, including but not limited to Solana, the Solana protocol, SPL Memo, SHA-256, AES, AES-256-GCM, ML-KEM, ML-KEM-768, HKDF, other cryptographic standards, JavaScript, TypeScript, Next.js, React, browser APIs, wallet software, RPC infrastructure, or any third-party library, dependency, trademark, or intellectual property. This License governs only material that the Licensor is legally entitled to license.

