1.1 **"License"** means this HashDrop Source-Available Reciprocal License, Version 1.0 (HSRL-1.0), including its definitions and all numbered Sections.

1.2 **"Licensor"** means HashDrop, the copyright holder identified in Section 38, including its successors-in-interest to the copyrights in the Covered Software.

1.3 **"Covered Software"** means the HashDrop source code, build and configuration files, documentation, and associated materials made available by the Licensor under this License, including this LICENSE file itself. Covered Software does **not** include Third-Party Components (Section 16) or any other material the Licensor is not legally entitled to license.

1.4 **"Modifications"** means any addition to, deletion from, or change to the contents of Covered Software, or any new file or work that contains or is derived from any part of Covered Software. Modifications include source code, build scripts, configuration changes, and documentation derived from Covered Software.

1.5 **"Covered Derivative"** means a work that constitutes a derivative work or adaptation of Covered Software under applicable copyright law, including: (a) Covered Software as modified by Modifications; (b) a new work into which a substantial portion of Covered Software has been copied, adapted, or incorporated; and (c) a combined or collective work in which portions of Covered Software remain identifiable. A Covered Derivative does **not** include:

(a) **Independent Code** (Section 1.6);

(b) works that merely communicate with, interoperate with, link to, reference, load data from, or exchange data with Covered Software or a Covered Derivative through public APIs, file formats, network protocols, or blockchain transactions, without copying or deriving from the structure, organization, or expression of Covered Software;

(c) separate works aggregated with Covered Software or a Covered Derivative on the same storage medium, repository, or distribution channel, where the separate works remain independent and separable ("mere aggregation"); or

(d) Third-Party Components.

1.6 **"Independent Code"** means software or other works that You author or own and that are not derived from Covered Software and are not Modifications, regardless of whether such code interoperates with, depends upon, communicates with, or is executed alongside Covered Software or a Covered Derivative.

1.7 **"Source Code Form"** means the preferred form of the Covered Software or a Covered Derivative for making modifications, including all source files and the scripts, interfaces, configuration files, and build and deployment instructions reasonably necessary to build and, where applicable, deploy the software from that source.

1.8 **"Object Code Form"** means any form of the Covered Software or a Covered Derivative other than Source Code Form, including compiled, bundled, minified, transpiled, or packaged forms.

1.9 **"Distribute"** (and its noun form **"Distribution"**) means to make Covered Software or a Covered Derivative available to any third party in Source Code Form or Object Code Form, whether by transfer of copies, publication, hosting for download, or making available through any medium. Running software for Your own permitted internal purposes is not a Distribution.

1.10 **"Network Service"** (or **"Hosted Service"**) means operating Covered Software or a Covered Derivative on a server, node, or other system so that third parties interact with it over a network without receiving a copy.

1.11 **"Commercial Use"** has the meaning given in Section 4.

1.12 **"You"** (or **"Recipient"**) means any individual or legal entity that exercises rights under this License.

1.13 **"Administrative and Provisioning Data"** means configuration data, credentials, secrets, encryption keys, signing keys, private keys, API keys, connection strings, personal information, customer data, third-party confidential information, and similar operational or business data. None of these are ever required to be disclosed under this License.

1.14 **"Official Release"** has the meaning given in Section 25.

1.15 **"Third-Party Components"** has the meaning given in Section 16.

1.16 **"Security Research"** has the meaning given in Section 17.

