## 6. Reciprocal Licensing Requirement

6.1 If You Distribute a Covered Derivative, in Source Code Form or Object Code Form, You must make the Covered Derivative available to all recipients under this License, or under another reciprocal source-available license expressly authorized in writing by the Licensor (a **"Compatible Reciprocal Arrangement"**).

6.2 The reciprocity obligation of Section 6.1 applies only to: (a) the Covered Software; and (b) Modifications. It does **not** apply to Independent Code, Third-Party Components, or Administrative and Provisioning Data, and it does not require the disclosure of any code or material that is not a Covered Derivative.

6.3 For clarity: communicating with, interoperating with, calling into, being called by, exchanging data with, or being distributed alongside Covered Software or a Covered Derivative does **not** by itself make a work a Covered Derivative. Ordinary interoperability, integration through public interfaces, and mere aggregation do not trigger the reciprocity obligation for unrelated works.

6.4 If You Distribute a Covered Derivative in Object Code Form, You must provide the corresponding Source Code Form as required by Section 7.

6.5 Because Distribution under this License is limited to non-commercial purposes, You must not condition receipt of a Covered Derivative on payment of a fee or other consideration; doing so constitutes Commercial Use subject to Section 4.

## 7. Source Code Requirements

7.1 Whenever this License requires Source Code Form to be made available, that source must be: (a) in the preferred form for making Modifications; (b) complete and corresponding to the exact Object Code Form Distributed or to the exact version operated as a Network Service; (c) in a machine-readable, non-proprietary format; and (d) accompanied by the build and deployment instructions reasonably necessary to produce the Object Code Form You Distributed or the functionality You operated.

7.2 Source Code Form may be made available: (a) together with the Distribution; (b) through a durable, publicly accessible network location identified with the Distribution; or (c) for Distribution on physical media, through a written offer valid for at least three (3) years.

7.3 Source Code Form made available under Sections 6, 7, or 8 must remain available for as long as You Distribute or operate the corresponding Covered Derivative, and in any event for at least three (3) years after Your last Distribution or operation of that version.

7.4 Making Source Code Form available under this Section does not require You to provide support, warranty, indemnity, or service levels for the Covered Derivative.

## 8. Network and Hosted Service Reciprocity

8.1 If You operate a Covered Derivative as a Network Service, You must make the Source Code Form of the Covered Software and of Your Modifications as used to operate that service reasonably available to the users of that service, under this License, at no charge beyond the cost of reproduction or network access, for as long as the service is operated. Availability may be satisfied through a prominent download location or a written offer delivered through the service.

8.2 The obligation in Section 8.1 covers the Covered Software and the Modifications used to provide the Network Service. It does **not** require You to disclose or make available:

(a) Independent Code;

(b) unrelated infrastructure, unrelated databases, unrelated proprietary systems, or unrelated internal tooling, including systems that merely host, deploy, monitor, or serve the Covered Derivative;

(c) Administrative and Provisioning Data, including private credentials, secrets, encryption keys, signing keys, API keys, and connection strings;

(d) customer data, personal information, or user content processed by the service; or

(e) third-party confidential information or Third-Party Components governed by their own licenses.

8.3 Operating **unmodified** Covered Software as a Network Service triggers the reciprocity obligation only with respect to Modifications, of which there are none in that case; any Commercial Use of such a service remains subject to Section 4.

8.4 The purpose of this Section is reciprocal availability of covered HashDrop-derived software. It is not intended to force disclosure of unrelated business infrastructure, and it must be interpreted accordingly.

